course: dictionary
lesson: 15578
title: Sweetened: sugar and more
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Sweetened» comes from the word sweet. When you sweeten a drink, you add sugar, honey or another sweet thing to it. «Mia sweetened her tea with a spoon of honey.» So sweetened means made sweet.
explain: The word can also be about things that are not food. «The shop sweetened the deal by adding a free pen.» Nothing in that sentence is sweet to eat. The shop made the offer better and more attractive, so sweetened means made more pleasant or more appealing.
explain: Look for clues around the word. If you see a drink, a cake or honey nearby, sugar was probably added. If you see a deal, an offer or a bonus, something was probably added to make it better. A good check is to swap in «made sweeter» and see if it still makes sense.
fact: «Sweetened» means made sweet by adding sugar, honey or another sweet thing.
fact: «Sweetened» can also mean made more pleasant or more attractive, like a deal with a bonus.
fact: «Unsweetened» means without any added sugar.
fact: Food labels may say «no added sugar» to show that a drink has not been sweetened.
fact: «Sweetened the deal» means added something to make an offer better.
exercise: «Dad sweetened his coffee with two spoons of sugar.» What does sweetened mean here? | Made cold and watery | Stirred very slowly | Spilled on the table | *Made sweet by adding sugar
exercise: «The bank sweetened the deal with a bonus.» What does sweetened suggest? | Made the offer smaller | *Made the offer more attractive | Made the bank sad | Made the deal sour
exercise: «The unsweetened tea tasted bitter.» Find and copy one word that means without added sugar. | *unsweetened | bitter | tea | tasted
test: «Ben's juice was sweetened, so it tasted very sugary.» What does sweetened mean? | Made sour with lemon | *Made sweet by adding something sweet | Poured into a glass | Kept cold in a fridge
test: Jess reads a label that says «no added sugar». She says the drink is unsweetened. Is she right? | *Yes, no sugar was added | Yes, the drink is full of sugar | No, the drink is very sweet | No, the drink is sour
exam: «The company sweetened its offer, so more people said yes.» What did the company do? | Made its offer smaller | *Made its offer more attractive | Stopped making its offer | Put its offer in a cake
